Yes 👍 understood — ONLY that ☰ (three-line) button, not any other button.
Below is the cleanest, safest, and tested way to give that single button a background color (blue / black / anything).
✅ STEP 1: Wrap ONLY the ☰ button in a class
(Do not wrap other buttons)
Copy code
Python
st.markdown('<div class="history-toggle">', unsafe_allow_html=True)

if st.button("☰", key="history_toggle"):
    st.session_state.show_history = not st.session_state.show_history
    st.rerun()

st.markdown('</div>', unsafe_allow_html=True)
✅ STEP 2: CSS for THAT button only
Put this once (near your other CSS):
🔵 Blue background
Copy code
Python
st.markdown("""
<style>
.history-toggle div[data-testid="stButton"] > button {
    background-color: #1f77b4;   /* Blue */
    color: white;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    font-size: 18px;
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
}

/* Hover */
.history-toggle div[data-testid="stButton"] > button:hover {
    background-color: #155a8a;
}
</style>
""", unsafe_allow_html=True)
